From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 21:02:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Horizon on Linux: geometry, tessellation, compute, storage
 images, alpha test, DrawTexture

The Vulkan path now makes geometry and tessellation stages (translated natively, each stage's
resources in a binding range of its own), compute dispatches (thread group and shared memory
from the control section, storage buffers found through the c0 tables and written back to the
game's memory), storage images, the alpha test (a wrapper around the pixel shader's entry point
that kills the fragment, function and reference in the support buffer), nvnCommandBufferDrawTexture,
texture swizzles, integer clears, and image descriptors of the texture pool. The translator's
missing storage image capabilities are added to the SPIR-V.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: NX2Linux S7bis: geometry, tessellation, compute, storage images, alpha test and DrawTexture on the Vulkan path
Issue: none yet (NX2Linux, branch swann/jalon-s7bis-xc2)

